course: dictionary
lesson: 803
title: Beg: asking very hard
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Beg means to ask for something so strongly, and so often, that it sounds like you really need it. The words around it show this. «The Mole begs him to stop» tells you the Mole is asking the Rat very hard to stop, because the list of food is too wonderful to hear any more.
explain: Beg can also mean asking strangers for money or food because you are poor. It can describe a dog too: the dog sits up with its front paws raised, hoping for a treat. Look at the words around beg to decide which meaning you need.
explain: Sven the reindeer in Frozen «begs for carrots». Sven is a reindeer, not a dog, and he is asking for something he wants a lot. Try your meaning in the sentence: does asking very hard for carrots still make sense? Yes, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Watch for phrases. «I beg your pardon» is a polite way to say sorry or to ask someone to say that again. «Beg for mercy» means asking for kindness when you are in trouble. A phrase can change the meaning, so read the whole group of words.
fact: Beg is a verb: beg, begs, begged, begging.
fact: «Beg» means to ask very strongly, again and again, for something you want a lot.
fact: «Beg» can mean asking strangers for money or food because you are poor.
fact: «Beg» can also mean a dog sitting up with its front paws raised, hoping for food or a treat.
fact: «I beg your pardon» is a polite way to say sorry or ask someone to repeat what they said.
exercise: «The Mole begs him to stop, because the food list is too wonderful.» What does begs mean here? | To run away quickly | To count every item on a list | To share a meal with friends | *To ask very hard, again and again
exercise: «The dog begs at the table, with its paws in the air.» What does begs mean? | To bark loudly at the postman | To ask strangers for money | *To sit up with its front paws raised, hoping for a treat
exercise: «I beg your pardon» is a polite way to say what? | Go away now | Please give me your money | *Sorry, or what did you say? | I promise to do better tomorrow
test:
Some people beg in the street because they are poor. What does beg mean here? | *To ask strangers for money or food because you are poor | To ask a teacher a question in class | To ask very hard for a later bedtime | To sit up with paws raised
Sven begs for carrots in Frozen. Which idea do you find in begs? | A character asking very hard for something he wants a lot | A reindeer sleeping in the snow | *A character asking very hard for something he wants a lot | A dog learning a new trick
exam: Which meaning fits «Ben sat up with his paws raised, hoping for a biscuit»? | To ask strangers for money | To ask very hard, again and again, for a later bedtime | *Of a dog: to sit up with its front paws raised, hoping for food
